# What this repository's em-dash scan leaves out, and why. One entry per line,
# anchored at the repository root; an entry ending in / covers every tracked path
# beneath it. An entry that matches no tracked path is refused rather than ignored,
# so this list cannot outlive its subject.
#
# THE VERBATIM BYTES OF A VENDORED PUBLICATION, and nothing else. The two directories
# below hold HL7's own files, committed byte for byte so the shipped structure registry
# can be derived offline and audited. One of them, the ACK-Scheduling structure, carries
# the JS escape spelling of the banned character inside HL7's own description text.
# There is no rewrite available: editing a vendored byte forfeits the whole point of
# vendoring it, and dropping that structure would change what the registry derives. The
# ban is a rule about prose that people write, and grounded data is not brand copy.
#
# THE EXCLUDED BYTES ARE NOT UNGUARDED, which is what makes this a narrowing rather than
# a hole. snapshot.json beside them records a sha256 for every one, and the parser
# structure provenance test recomputes all of them, so a file edited to smuggle anything
# in reds the suite.
#
# IT IS THESE TWO SUBDIRECTORIES AND NOTHING ELSE. This repository's own writing under
# the vendor tree (its README, its snapshot) is still scanned, so a person cannot put
# prose behind this exclusion by choosing a directory. This file is scanned like any
# other tracked file and excludes nothing on its own behalf.
vendor/hl7-v2ig/message-structure/
vendor/hl7-v2ig/control-manifests/

# THE CHANGELOG. Every entry above "Released before this file was generated" is written by the
# release tool from a changeset, and every changeset passes this same scan before it can merge, so
# new text is already covered. Below that heading is the frozen archive of releases before the tool,
# which is never hand-edited and holds en dashes in its history. The shared gate excludes by exact
# path, not by heading, so the whole file is listed.
CHANGELOG.md

# VERBATIM ROWS FROM THE HL7 V2-TO-FHIR IMPLEMENTATION GUIDE, used as test fixtures. Like the
# vendored files above, these are grounded data, copied byte for byte, not prose we write.
test/fixtures/fhir-bridge/ig-segment-maps/OBR-DiagnosticReport.csv
test/fixtures/fhir-bridge/ig-segment-maps/OBX-Observation.csv
